    <!-- ===================== SECTION 6: TOURS ===================== -->
    <section style="padding-top: 2rem;">

      <!-- Section head and intro note — padded -->
      <div class="mob-pad" style="padding-left: 4rem; padding-right: 4rem; padding-bottom: 0;">

        <header style="padding-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <p style="font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--ink-light); font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 300; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Tours</p>
          <h2 style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; line-height: 1.2;">San Francisco's history, mysteries, and the Bay itself.</h2>
          <p style="font-size: 18.75px; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 300; font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-mid); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">A quiet garden, a windswept bay, a neighborhood with three hidden histories, one of the city's most enigmatic founders, and the cycles of discovery, innovation, and disruption that have reinvented San Francisco and the world again and again. Riveting stories that will make you glad you came.</p>
        </header>

        <p style="font-size: 18.75px; font-style: italic; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-light); font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; padding: 0.75rem 0 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">All tours run through San Francisco City Guides — a nonprofit program of the San Francisco Public Library. Every walk is free; donations support the program. Private tours are also available — ideal for work groups, family visits, or custom experiences. I lead the tours below, but the full City Guides schedule has outstanding guides across the whole city. Book whatever calls to you.</p>

      </div>

      <!-- Tour 1: Maritime San Francisco — image LEFT -->
      <article class="tour-card">
        <div class="tour-card-image">
          <img src="/images/maritime.webp" alt="A tall ship under full sail passing the Golden Gate Bridge">
        </div>
        <div class="tour-card-text">
          <p class="tour-written-by">Tour written by Eric</p>
          <h3 class="tour-name">Maritime San Francisco</h3>
          <p class="tour-desc">A tour of the City by the Bay that finally gives the Bay its due. History and culture woven together with whatever is actually unfolding in front of us — boardsport athletes, racing sailboats, Coast Guard vessels, fishing boats. I spend a fair amount of time on the water myself, and it shows.</p>
          <p class="tour-media">Featured by <a href="https://www.latitude38.com/lectronic/2025/09/29/#guided-walk-san-francisco-maritime-past-present" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Latitude 38</a></p>
          <div class="tour-buttons">
            <a href="https://sfcityguides.org/tour/maritime-sf/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">View Schedule</a>
            <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nv8yu3_P6hR9_ZF9g5GAbupsVxdPJjTW5kXbAxRJu-U/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">Nearby Recommendations</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Tour 2: 1840s San Francisco — image RIGHT -->
      <article class="tour-card tour-card-reverse">
        <div class="tour-card-image">
          <img src="/images/1840s.webp" alt="1840s San Francisco">
        </div>
        <div class="tour-card-text">
          <p class="tour-written-by">Tour written by Eric</p>
          <h3 class="tour-name">1840s San Francisco &amp; the Legacy of America's First Black Millionaire</h3>
          <p class="tour-desc">I built this tour from scratch, hunting through archives for clues about a remarkable and shockingly undervalued figure in California history. The story is intriguing; the story of the story takes it even further. The research also became my book.</p>
          <p class="tour-media">Featured on <a href="https://www.kalw.org/show/state-bay/2025-08-24/valkyries-vibes-bay-area-unified-americas-first-black-millionaire" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KALW 91.7</a> and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_pXELxaVHCI" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CBS Bay Area</a></p>
          <div class="tour-buttons">
            <a href="https://sfcityguides.org/tour/1840s-san-francisco-and-the-astonishing-legacy-of-americas-first-black-millionaire/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">View Schedule</a>
            <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LfxVYSsd9saJUW4UQYjZLLTT0lX6fz7hfk51dBmFHas" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">Nearby Recommendations</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Tour 3: Japanese Tea Garden — image LEFT -->
      <article class="tour-card">
        <div class="tour-card-image">
          <img src="/images/japaneseteagarden.webp" alt="The Japanese Tea Garden, Golden Gate Park">
        </div>
        <div class="tour-card-text">
          <h3 class="tour-name">Japanese Tea Garden</h3>
          <p class="tour-desc">People who wander in without intending to take a tour often end up staying for the whole experience. The oldest continuously operating public Japanese garden outside of Japan, the Garden was created for the 1894 Midwinter Fair. It is transformed when someone shows you how to read it: botany, history, horticulture, spiritual depth, and the iconic structures that will earn their place in your memory and photo stream.</p>
          <aside class="tour-bracket-aside">This Garden and I go deeper than the tours. After studying the Main Gate's traditional bracket system, I built a scale model of one of its roof brackets — displayed at the Garden and at the Kezuroukai woodworking gathering. The project and photos are <a href="https://justwood.design/work/tokyo-bracket/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">on my woodworking site</a>.</aside>
          <div class="tour-buttons">
            <a href="https://sfcityguides.org/tour/japanese-tea-garden/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">View Schedule</a>
            <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lhsKlREKSpnU_VCr_fmnfQz0kgdz-dH3e71h3T1Eow4/edit" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">Nearby Recommendations</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Tour 4: Boom and Bust — image RIGHT -->
      <article class="tour-card tour-card-reverse">
        <div class="tour-card-image">
          <img src="/images/boomandbust.webp" alt="San Francisco Financial District">
        </div>
        <div class="tour-card-text">
          <h3 class="tour-name">Boom and Bust</h3>
          <p class="tour-desc">Gold Rush. Silver Rush. Dot Com. Today's AI boom. The plummets into panic, racial violence, and displacement. A sweeping yet focused look at the city's economic rhythms from the 1840s to today — history that rhymes loudly with the present. As a veteran of the tech industry, I bring particular insight into how that sector has shaped and continues to shape the region. Especially compelling as a private tour for work groups.</p>
          <div class="tour-buttons">
            <a href="https://sfcityguides.org/tour/san-francisco-boom-bust/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">View Schedule</a>
            <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sEy2sdILs1GU-u7tZVMsL388FAE-ZppbOpQP-BVCQdA" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">Nearby Recommendations</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Tour 5: Japantown — image LEFT -->
      <article class="tour-card">
        <div class="tour-card-image">
          <img src="/images/japantown.webp" alt="Japantown, San Francisco">
        </div>
        <div class="tour-card-text">
          <h3 class="tour-name">Japantown</h3>
          <p class="tour-desc">San Francisco's Japantown — one of only three remaining in the US, and the largest and oldest — is also the city's most layered neighborhood, once called "the Little United Nations." Jewish, Japanese, and Black American communities each made a home here, in a neighborhood always already in flux. Food culture, public art, comparative religions, and surprising cultural crossovers. Lots of good places to eat nearby too.</p>
          <div class="tour-buttons">
            <a href="https://sfcityguides.org/tour/japantown/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">View Schedule</a>
            <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L7WFtLzVNASo6L24OwwiKGq-d2MUAIKTxcJtW2lEZDU/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tour">Nearby Recommendations</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </section>

    <!-- ===================== SECTION 7: SCHEDULE BANNER ===================== -->
    <div class="mob-pad" style="padding-left: 4rem; padding-right: 4rem; padding-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="background: var(--parchment-dark); border: 1px solid var(--parchment-deep); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem; margin: 2.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; line-height: 1.3;">Ready to walk?</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 18.75px; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-mid); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1rem;">My personal tour calendar shows exactly when I'm leading — but you'll need to head to the San Francisco City Guides website to book. Once there, look for Eric F. on the schedule.</p>

        <div
          x-data="{
            events: [],
            async init() {
              const icalUrl = 'REDACTED_ICAL_URL';
              if (!icalUrl) return;
              try {
                const res = await fetch(icalUrl);
                if (!res.ok) return;
                const text = await res.text();
                const jcal = ICAL.parse(text);
                const comp = new ICAL.Component(jcal);
                const vevents = comp.getAllSubcomponents('vevent');
                const now = new Date();
                const upcoming = vevents
                  .map(ev => {
                    const e = new ICAL.Event(ev);
                    return {
                      start: e.startDate.toJSDate(),
                      summary: e.summary
                    };
                  })
                  .filter(e => e.start >= now)
                  .sort((a, b) => a.start - b.start);
                this.events = upcoming.map(e => {
                  const day = e.start.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { weekday: 'long', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
                  const time = e.start.toLocaleTimeString('en-US', { hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit' });
                  return day + ' — ' + e.summary + ' — ' + time;
                });
              } catch(err) {
                // silently fail — no events shown
              }
            }
          }"
        >
          <div x-show="events.length > 0" x-cloak style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            <template x-for="event in events" :key="event">
              <p x-text="event" style="font-size: 18.75px; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; color: var(--ink-mid); margin: 0.2rem 0;"></p>
            </template>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
          <a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/embed?src=aldkllofa2m63nlbo4rca9lscu31mm52%40import.calendar.google.com&ctz=America%2FLos_Angeles" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">My personal schedule →</a>
          <a href="https://sfcityguides.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-outline">Book on City Guides →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ===================== SECTION 8: BEYOND THE TOUR ===================== -->
    <section style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 2rem; padding-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div class="mob-pad" style="padding-left: 4rem; padding-right: 4rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--ink-light); font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 300; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">Beyond the Tour</p>
        <h2 style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.2;">When I'm not walking</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 18.75px; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-mid); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 0.9rem;">I'm a Berkeley-based artist, craftsman, and writer. My woodworking practice — Japanese joinery, furniture, turned and carved objects — lives at <a href="https://justwood.design" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(139,58,26,0.3);">justwood.design</a>. I enjoy drawing and painting in various media. I spend as much time as possible in, on, and under the water.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 18.75px; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-mid); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0;">The same impulse drives all of it: curiosity about how things come together, and why they matter.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

